#horizontalrule

== Upon Whom is Qurbānī Obligatory?
<upon-whom-qurbani>

=== Basic Criteria
<basic-criteria>
The person must be: (1) #strong[Muslim], (2) #strong[ʿĀqil] (sane),
(3) #strong[Bāligh] (mature).

=== Specific Criteria for Qurbānī
<specific-criteria>
In addition: (4) #strong[Muqīm] (resident, not a musāfir), and
(5) #strong[Ṣāḥib al-Niṣāb] --- owner of niṣāb amount beyond basic
needs (#strong[ḥājāt aṣliyyah]).

The niṣāb is the value of #strong[612+ grams of silver] (the lower
of the two thresholds of gold and silver).

#horizontalrule

=== Two Key Differences from Zakāt Niṣāb
<differences-from-zakat>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: 3,
    align: (auto, auto, auto),
    table.header([Point], [Zakāt], [Qurbānī / Ṣadaqat al-Fiṭr]),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Ḥawl (year)]],
    [Required --- niṣāb must be held for one full year],
    [#strong[Not required] --- even acquiring niṣāb on the last day
    of Eid before sunset makes Qurbānī wājib],
    [#strong[Exemptions]],
    [Broader --- e.g., a backup car (not for trade) is not counted],
    [#strong[Narrower] --- backup car, extra house not in use, etc.
    are counted toward niṣāb],
  )]
  , kind: table
)

#horizontalrule

=== Women and Qurbānī
<women-and-qurbani>
Qurbānī is #strong[individually obligatory] upon women who meet the
niṣāb, even if their only asset is jewelry.

- If she has #strong[only gold] (no other assets): the niṣāb of
  #strong[gold] must be completed.
- If she has a #strong[mixture] (gold + cash, gold + silver, etc.):
  the niṣāb of #strong[silver] (the lower threshold) is used.

#strong[Practical advice:] Women should plan for Qurbānī throughout the
year (e.g., saving a small daily amount), rather than scrambling on Eid
day. The husband commonly takes this burden, which is permissible ---
but it must be done #strong[with the wife's knowledge].

=== One Qurbānī per Person, Not per Family
<one-per-person>
A common misconception: one Qurbānī suffices for the whole family. This
is #strong[incorrect] in the Ḥanafī school. Every individual who meets
all the criteria must have their own Qurbānī.

#horizontalrule

=== Debt and Niṣāb
<debt-and-nisab>
Debt is deducted from total assets. For #strong[long-term loans] (home
loans, etc.), only the #strong[yearly installment due] is deducted ---
not the entire loan amount.

=== No Qurbānī on Minors or Insane Persons
<no-qurbani-minors>
There is no Qurbānī obligation on an immature child or a majnūn,
regardless of their wealth. However, it is #strong[recommended] for a
wealthy father to perform Qurbānī on behalf of his immature children.

=== Poor Person Who Buys an Animal
<poor-person-buys>
If a poor person purchases an animal #strong[with the intention of
Qurbānī], the Qurbānī becomes #strong[wājib] upon him on account of
that purchase.

#horizontalrule

== Days and Timing of Qurbānī
<days-timing-qurbani>

=== Three Days
<three-days>
The days of slaughtering are the #strong[10th, 11th, and 12th of Dhul
Ḥijjah]. The first day is the best.

- Slaughtering at #strong[night] is #strong[makrūh].
- Time technically begins after #strong[Fajr] on the 10th (Sharʿī
  daytime begins at Fajr, not sunrise).

=== In Cities (Where Eid Prayer is Performed)
<in-cities>
Slaughtering #strong[must be done after the Eid prayer]. If done before,
the Qurbānī is #strong[not valid] and must be repeated (the meat is
still ḥalāl, but the wājib is not fulfilled).

If there are multiple masjids: once the #strong[first masjid] in the
city completes its Eid prayer, slaughtering is permissible for the
entire city.

=== In Small Villages (No Eid Prayer)
<in-villages>
Slaughtering may be done immediately #strong[after Fajr].

#strong[Practical shortcut:] A person in the city can send his animal to
a nearby village (where no Eid prayer is performed) to be slaughtered
after Fajr, then have the meat brought back. The #strong[place of the
animal] determines the ruling.

#horizontalrule

== Sending Qurbānī Abroad
<sending-abroad>
When Qurbānī is sent to another country, it must be performed on a
#strong[common Eid day] --- a day that is a valid Eid day in #strong[both]
the animal's location and the person's location.

- If Eid in the US is Wednesday and in India is Thursday, the Qurbānī
  in India must be done on #strong[Thursday].
- It should not be done on a day that would be the 13th in the person's
  location (as that exceeds the valid days).

#horizontalrule

== Charity Cannot Replace Qurbānī
<charity-cannot-replace>
No amount of ṣadaqah can replace Qurbānī. ʿIbādāt are fixed by Allah's
command, not by human logic.

#horizontalrule

== Animals for Qurbānī
<animals-for-qurbani>

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: 3,
    align: (auto, auto, auto),
    table.header([Category], [Animals], [Shares]),
    table.hline(),
    [Small animals], [Goat, sheep, ram, lamb], [1 share (1 animal =
    1 person)],
    [Cattle], [Cow, buffalo, ox], [Up to 7 shares],
    [Camel], [Camel], [Up to 7 shares],
