- Only #strong[domesticated livestock] of the above types are valid.
  Wild animals --- even if kept as pets --- are not valid.
- The validity of buffalo for Qurbānī is established in Ḥanafī fiqh
  (objections by some groups were addressed by Mawlānā Yūsuf
  Ludhyānwī).

#horizontalrule

== Partnerships in Larger Animals --- Critical Rulings
<partnerships-critical>

=== All Partners Must Intend ʿIbādah
<partners-ibadah>
Every partner's share must be for an act of #strong[ʿibādah] ---
whether Qurbānī, Walīmah, ʿAqīqah, or similar. If even #strong[one
partner] has no ʿibādah intention, the Qurbānī of #strong[all partners]
is invalidated.

=== The Ḥarām Income Problem
<haram-income>
If one partner's income is #strong[majority ḥarām] and he pays his
share from ḥarām earnings, the Qurbānī is #strong[invalid for all
partners].

#strong[Rules for assessment:]
- If there is #strong[no evidence] against a partner, the default
  assumption is #strong[ḥalāl] --- benefit of the doubt applies.
- Assessment is based on #strong[ẓāhir] (apparent situation).
- You are not required to investigate deeply, but you #strong[must not
  knowingly] partner with someone whose majority income is ḥarām.
- For #strong[mixed income] (e.g., gas station selling both ḥalāl and
  ḥarām items): the #strong[majority] of income is assessed.

#strong[When using Qurbānī services] where partners are assigned by the
organization: benefit of the doubt applies as long as you have no
specific evidence of a problem.

